\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. To Thee, O Lord, our hearts we raise
\par In hymns of adoration,
\par To Thee bring sacrifice of praise
\par With shouts of exultation;
\par Bright robes of gold the fields adorn,
\par The hills with joy are ringing,
\par The valleys stand so thick with corn
\par That even they are singing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. And now, on this our festal day,
\par Thy bounteous hand confessing,
\par Before Thee thankfully we lay
\par The first- fruits of Thy blessing.
\par By Thee the souls of men are fed
\par With gifts of grace supernal;
\par Thou who dost give us earthly bread,
\par Give us the bread eternal.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We bear the burden of the day,
\par And often toil seems dreary;
\par But labour ends with sunset ray,
\par And rest comes for the weary;
\par May we, the angel- reaping o'er,
\par Stand at the last accepted,
\par Christ's golden sheaves for evermore
\par To garners bright elected.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O blessed is that land of God
\par Where saints abide for ever,
\par Where golden fields spread far and broad,
\par Where flows the crystal river,
\par The strains of all its holy  throng
\par With ours to- day are blending;
\par Thrice blessed is that harvest song
\par Which never hath an ending.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

